<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/tu_0001/locator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/Locator> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/na_0012> <http://digistrucmed.org/hasSourceGradeRecord> <http://digistrucmed.org/grade-record/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/gr_0013> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/tu_0013> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "Nutraceutical use is not recommended for relief of symptomatic HF or for the secondary prevention of cardiovascular events. Patients should be instructed to avoid using natural or synthetic products containing ephedra (ma huang), ephedrine, or its metabolites because of an increase risk of mortality and morbidity. Products should be avoided that may have significant drug interactions with digoxin, vasodilators, beta blockers, antiarrhythmic drugs, and anticoagulants. (Strength of Evidence = B)" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/na_0002> <http://digistrucmed.org/patientApplicability> "UNCONDITIONAL_WITHIN_STATED_POPULATION" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/tricyclic%20antidepressants> <http://digistrucmed.org/name> "tricyclic antidepressants" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/normative-assertion/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/na_0014> <http://digistrucmed.org/operation> "DOCUMENT" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/entity-mention/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/e_0009> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://digistrucmed.org/Drug> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/Anatomy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://digistrucmed.org/grade-record/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/gr_0004> <http://digistrucmed.org/rawGrade> "C" .
<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_2b6290b9ec9e0199863d75426f4eb32800b1dbc4c89274d4f3da3dea703a1dad_n0029/tu_0003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ARBs are recommended for asymptomatic patients with reduced LVEF who are intolerant of ACE inhibitors from cough or angioedema. (Strength of Evidence = C)" .
